{"name":"Bronze Mist","hex":"#a37f44","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"},{"term":"mist","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water or other liquid finely suspended in air.","A layer of fine droplets or particles."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form mist.","To spray fine droplets on, particularly of water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Mist","blocks":[{"text":"Mist is a natural phenomenon caused by small droplets of water aerosols suspended in the cold air, usually by condensation. Physically, it is an example of a dispersion, most commonly seen where water vapor in warm, moist air meets sudden cooling, such as in exhaled air in the winter, or when hot sauna steam is suddenly released outside. Mist occurs naturally as part of weather, typically when humid air comes into contact with surfaces that are much cooler. It can also be created artificially with aerosol spray dispensers if the humidity and temperature conditions are right."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg/330px-%D0%97%D0%B0_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D0%BC_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mist","wikidata":"Q192196"},{"title":"Bronze (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is a metallic brown color which resembles the metal alloy bronze. An archaic term for it was aeneous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png/330px-Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_(color)","wikidata":"Q2778382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statue